WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:02.736
This morning.

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:04.471
Officials in Ukraine putting extra

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.705
security measures in place.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:06.706
They fear

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.975
Russia will ramp up attacks to mark

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.077
the one year anniversary tomorrow.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:11.611
Joining us now

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.645
to speak about the state of the war,

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:13.279
retired U.S.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:14.581
Air Force General Philip Breedlove.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.548
He's the former

00:00:15.548 --> 00:00:17.384
NATO supreme allied commander.

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:18.284
Also distinguished here

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:19.285
for the Middle East Institute.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.021
Good to have you on sir.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.857
Good to be back.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.558
So we're a hearing tomorrow

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.061
to the formal invasion of the East.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.864
There had been some hope in recent months

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:31.431
that perhaps

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.065
Vladimir Putin

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:34.067
would see the writing on the wall here,

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.602
maybe shoot for peace.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.169
A lot of hope,

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:36.836
but some hope,

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.371
but clearly not given

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.272
his comments lately.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:41.574
And devotion of further resources

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.009
and forces there.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.911
Do you see any end in sight to this war?

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.883
Well, not right now.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:50.817
Clearly, Mr.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:54.320
Putin also has his back against the wall.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.922
He can't come

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.123
out of this war

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.225
with less land than he entered.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.061
And while the fight

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.996
is not existential to Russia,

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.398
it may be existential to him.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.232
On the other side.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.801
President Zelensky

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.869
is enjoying strong,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.970
incredibly strong

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.306
and growing support among his people

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.976
to take back all of Ukrainian land.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.178
So right now,

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.047
we are truly at loggerheads.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.582
General, there's so much concern

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.583
and fear that

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.217
President Putin

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:25.552
is going to use tomorrow

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:28.321
use this one year anniversary

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.856
to launch some sort of new offensive,

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:32.692
do something big and symbolic in Ukraine.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.295
Do you think that's going to happen?

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.298
Well, most will tell you,

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:38.731
I believe

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.200
now that this offensive

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.901
has already begun.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.070
It's not going in the way Mr.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.172
Putin would want it. To go.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.142
So I think the offensive is already on.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.078
But will he try something flashy?

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.247
That's not beyond him.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.449
The Russians are very keen to sort of

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.585
celebrate anniversaries.

00:01:58.585 --> 00:01:59.552
And so

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.955
I think that Ukraine is standing ready

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.656
in case that does happen.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:05.325
Does Russia have the

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.461
capability to do to bleed attempt

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.163
to bleed Ukraine to

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.397
to keep at this here

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.365
in this war of attrition?

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.200
And does Ukraine, in your view,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.804
have the capability to stand up to that

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:19.839
Well, Mr.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:20.940
Putin intends

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.077
to give us the message that he will stay.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.346
And I'll use your words, not my words.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.947
Bleed Ukraine

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.750
because he knows he has the autocratic

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:31.918
or, as I say,

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.786
kleptocratic power

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.555
to make those kinds of decisions.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.658
And he's counting on the leadership

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:42.162
of the West to grow tired and to weaken.

00:02:42.162 --> 00:02:43.029
And so

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.198
I think that's his every intention.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:46.799
Ukraine.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.536
If we give them what they need, they

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:50.703
beat Russia

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.772
every time on the battlefield.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.642
Two strategic defeat in the north

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.911
and on the verge of an operational

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.612
level defeat in the south.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.780
So Ukraine

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:01.681
stands ready

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.750
as long as the West will give

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.651
them what they need.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.320
Well, General Philip

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.755
Breedlove, it's good to have you on.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:09.622
Certainly a conversation

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:10.924
will keep up in the coming days

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.325
and weeks as we monitor the war there.

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.393
Thanks for joining us this morning.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:14.661
Thank you, General.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.130
Well, CNN is also getting

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:17.664
a firsthand

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:19.832
look inside that battered town

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:21.534
in southeastern Ukraine.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.669
CNN's Alex Marquardt

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.871
filed this report for us

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.707
this fight for bullied

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:28.174
are right

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:29.776
now is one of the most important

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.311
and difficult in the country.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.912
While the fight for a back

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.914
mood is largely symbolic,

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.116
This is a very strategic fight

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.484
for both sides.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:39.752
Vali Da is unique

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:40.587
in that it sits

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:41.554
at the intersection

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.591
of the two main active fronts in Ukraine.

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:46.759
The Southern and the eastern front.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.061
That is why Russia

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.963
wants to try to push through here

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:52.398
to launch an offensive into Donbass.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.233
It is believed that

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.867
this is one of their shaping

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.603
operations, the beginning

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:58.004
of a larger offensive

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:00.206
to come in the next few weeks.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:03.042
But they are struggling very badly

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:03.543
right now.

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.311
They've lost a huge amount of men

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.479
and armored vehicles

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:07.914
as they try to cross

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.016
open fields, including minefields,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.718
where the Ukrainians

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:12.552
have been able

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:14.654
to inflict a huge amount of damage

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:15.655
on their troops.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.056
At the same time,

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:20.360
the Russians are absolutely pummeling

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.327
this town.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.895
You can see all around me.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.330
These are Soviet era,

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.166
a apartment blocks now largely empty.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.768
The residents have fled.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:31.237
And almost every single one

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.274
destroyed in varying degrees.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.909
All of the windows have been blown out.

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:40.113
Craters here in the ground where children

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:41.981
used to play.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:44.250
Ukrainians have the benefit

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.019
of the higher ground here

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.253
and these buildings

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.188
to use in the fighting.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.190
But as with so many of the battles

00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:53.092
here in eastern Ukraine,

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.528
it is a fight of attrition

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.430
who can hold out the longest.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.865
The Ukrainian side saying

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.633
they need more ammunition

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.067
to be able

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.935
to keep the Russians at bay,

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.071
to keep them from advancing.

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.539
Alex Marquardt, CNN,

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:07.840
border in eastern Ukraine.

